#: Score/AnalysisResultDetailAdapter.php:41
#, fuzzy
msgid "DMARC, or Domain-based Message Authentication, Reporting, and Conformance, is an email authentication protocol that allows domain owners to protect their domain from unauthorized use, such as spam and phishing attacks. It is important because it helps protect against these types of cyber threats and helps ensure the authenticity of emails from a specific domain. This helps prevent email spoofing, which is when attackers send emails that appear to be from a legitimate source but are actually fraudulent. DMARC also provides reporting and feedback mechanisms to help domain owners monitor and improve their email authentication practices."
msgstr "I-DMARC, noma i-Domain-based Message Authentication, Ukubika, kanye ne-Conformance, yi-protocol yokuqinisekisa i-imeyili evumela abanikazi besizinda ukuthi bavikele isizinda sabo ekusetshenzisweni okungagunyaziwe, njengokuhlaselwa kogaxekile nokukhwabanisa. Kubalulekile ngoba kusiza ukuvikela lezi zinhlobo zezinsongo ze-cyber futhi kusiza ukuqinisekisa ubuqiniso be-imeyili kusuka kusizinda esithile. Lokhu kusiza ukuvimbela i-imeyili spoofing, okuyilapho abahlaseli bethumela ama-imeyili abonakala evela kumthombo osemthethweni kodwa empeleni akhohlisa. I-DMARC iphinde inikeze izindlela zokubika kanye nempendulo ukusiza abanikazi besizinda ukuqapha nokuthuthukisa imikhuba yabo yokuqinisekisa i-imeyili."

#: Score/AnalysisResultDetailAdapter.php:43
#, fuzzy
msgid "A sender policy framework (SPF) is a security protocol that helps prevent email spoofing by verifying the sender's identity and ensuring that the email is being sent from an authorized server. This is important because email spoofing is a common tactic used by cybercriminals to send fraudulent or malicious emails that appear to be from legitimate sources, such as a bank or government agency. SPF helps to protect individuals and organizations from these types of scams, by ensuring that the sender's identity is authentic and the email is coming from a trusted source."
msgstr "Uhlaka lwenqubomgomo yomthumeli (i-SPF) yi-protocol yokuphepha esiza ukuvimbela ukukhwabanisa nge-imeyili ngokuqinisekisa ubunikazi bomthumeli nokuqinisekisa ukuthi i-imeyili ithunyelwa kusuka kwiseva egunyaziwe. Lokhu kubalulekile ngoba i-imeyili spoofing iyindlela evamile esetshenziswa ngama-cybercriminals ukuthumela ama-imeyili akhohlisayo noma anonya abonakala evela emithonjeni esemthethweni, njengebhange noma inhlangano kahulumeni. I-SPF isiza ukuvikela abantu kanye nezinhlangano kulezi zinhlobo zokukhwabanisa, ngokuqinisekisa ukuthi ubunikazi bomthumeli buyiqiniso futhi i-imeyili ivela kumthombo othembekile."

#: Score/AnalysisResultDetailAdapter.php:45
#, fuzzy
msgid "DKIM (DomainKeys Identified Mail) is an email authentication technique that uses a digital signature to verify that an email message has not been altered during transit. It is important because it helps protect against spam, phishing, and other types of email fraud. By verifying the authenticity of an email message, DKIM helps ensure that the sender is who they claim to be, and that the message has not been tampered with. This helps to prevent malicious actors from sending fake or fraudulent emails that could potentially harm the recipient. Overall, DKIM is an important tool for securing email communications and protecting against cyber threats."
msgstr "I-DKIM (DomainKeys Identified Mail) iyindlela yokuqinisekisa i-imeyili esebenzisa isignesha yedijithali ukuqinisekisa ukuthi umyalezo we-imeyili awuzange uguqulwe ngesikhathi sokuthutha. Kubalulekile ngoba kusiza ukuvikela ugaxekile, ukukhwabanisa, nezinye izinhlobo zokukhwabanisa nge-imeyili. Ngokuqinisekisa ubuqiniso bomlayezo we-imeyili, i-DKIM isiza ukuqinisekisa ukuthi umthumeli ungubani abathi ungubani, nokuthi umyalezo awuzange uphazanyiswe. Lokhu kusiza ukuvimbela abadlali abanonya ekuthumeleni ama-imeyili amanga noma okukhwabanisa angalimaza umamukeli. Sekukonke, i-DKIM iyithuluzi elibalulekile lokuvikela ukuxhumana nge-imeyili nokuvikela izinsongo ze-cyber."

#: Score/AnalysisResultDetailAdapter.php:47
#, fuzzy
msgid "Domain age refers to the length of time that a domain name has been registered and in use. It is important for the domain reputation because older domains tend to have a better reputation and are generally more trustworthy. This is because older domains have had more time to establish themselves, build up a positive online presence, and develop a good reputation. Additionally, newer domains are often considered less credible and authoritative because they didn’t have the time to build an audience."
msgstr "Ubudala besizinda bubhekisela e ubude besikhathi lapho igama lesizinda libhaliswe futhi lisetshenziswa. Kubalulekile kwidumela lesizinda ngoba izizinda ezindala zivame ukuba nedumela elingcono futhi ngokuvamile zithembekile kakhulu. Lokhu kungenxa yokuthi izizinda ezindala ziye zaba nesikhathi esiningi sokuzisungula, ukwakha ubukhona obuhle be-intanethi, nokuthuthukisa idumela elihle. Ngaphezu kwalokho, izizinda ezintsha zivame ukubhekwa njengezingathembekile futhi ezinegunya ngoba azizange zibe nesikhathi sokwakha izilaleli."

